{
  "kind": "mip0018-case",
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "C06",
  "title": "Minimal OwnerKey (kind 3, no OpenZeppelin) lifecycle: deploy, publish, rename, withdraw (one Null record at name), withdraw again, revive",
  "demonstrates": "MIP \"Applying records\" on chain: latest value wins (S2); a Null record at `name` deletes only `name` — the identity keeps symbol, decimals and standards (S3a); a repeated Null at `name` changes nothing (S3b); a later record sets the field again and nothing from before the Null returns (the revive sets name and symbol; decimals and standards were never deleted).",
  "conclusion": "after withdraw (and withdraw again): no name; symbol \"ACMP\", decimals 6, standards \"mip-0004\", group \"ACMP\"; final: name \"Acme Again\", symbol \"ACMA\", decimals 6, standards \"mip-0004\" (group \"ACMA\"); the A1 publish payload equals MIP Appendix A byte-for-byte.",
  "mip": {
    "commit": "274a84f221bcfc17e4b73e2c8b32fd8c028ea092",
    "eventName": "mip-0018:token-metadata[v1]"
  },
  "source": {
    "example": "examples/minimal",
    "contract": "examples/minimal/contracts/OwnerKey.compact",
    "metadata": "examples/minimal/owner-key.metadata.json",
    "deployedFrom": "examples/minimal/contracts/OwnerKey.compact at 70b54c674260b13c0cdbf1df72457f77a3dba2fe: its withdrawMetadata() emits one Null record at name (verifier key ba50827a038885613c531250ba02d301c82fe44ed8c555f5c9b36dd3576d1917, record.json)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "This deployment's withdrawMetadata() emits one Null record at `name` (source: examples/minimal/contracts/OwnerKey.compact at 70b54c6), so the case shows a single-key delete: decimals and standards stay, and the revive sets a name and a new symbol next to them. examples/minimal/contracts/OwnerKey.compact in this tree emits a Null record for each of the four keys; case C11 deploys it.",
    "OwnerKey renames with setMetadata(name, symbol), so the revive sets name and symbol (10- and 4-byte values: \"Acme Again\"/\"ACMA\").",
    "Every intermediate state is re-checkable: `recheck` lists the contract as of each step's block (`list --to-block`)."
  ],
  "placeholders": {
    "{net}": "network options (Stagenet: --network stagenet)",
    "{signer}": "wallet 1's signer options (mnemonic file, wallet cache)",
    "{signer2}": "wallet 2's signer options, with its OWN private-state file",
    "{case}": "this case folder",
    "{out}": "where records and observations are written (Stagenet: this case folder)",
    "{out:<ID>}": "another case's output folder"
  },
